{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011Cfu1gdYr2PF6N7C1D5N76","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"**Build it, but as a small, measured rollout with a randomized holdout. Don't do a separate research phase first.**\n\n**Why build:** The email result is strong evidence. It was randomized, so the 13-point drop (31% to 18%) is causal. With about 400 patients per arm, it's too big to be noise. Reminding people works, and push is another way to deliver the reminder. Three weeks of two engineers is cheap compared with a research phase that would mostly re-learn this.\n\n**What's uncertain:** Whether the email effect carries over to push.\n- The trial only covered patients who opted in to email, who may be more engaged than average.\n- Push reaches only people who have the app and have allowed notifications. That group may differ from email opt-ins, and it may overlap heavily with them.\n- Push is easier to dismiss, so the effect could be smaller. It could also be larger.\n\n**How to handle it:**\n1. Before building, check how many repeat-prescription patients have the app with push enabled. If that's small, the payoff is small and the decision changes. This is a data pull, not research.\n2. Ship push with a permanent randomized holdout, for example 10–20% of eligible patients who get no push. Stratify by whether they also get email. This makes the build the experiment.\n3. Write down the decision rule now. For example: if push gives less than a 3-point drop in late collection beyond what email already achieves, stop investing.\n4. Reuse the email reminder's timing and content. Don't redesign them in this project.\n\n**Main risk:** Push may mostly reach patients who already get the email, so its added value could be small. The stratified holdout will show this."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3452,"cache_read_input_tokens":5027,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3452},"output_tokens":4,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"1b541c93-32b5-48c9-858b-86e9d9195a7b","uuid":"fefe73e0-3546-4cb2-90e8-d13cc35597a8","timestamp":"2026-10-10T18:15:26.456Z","request_id":"req_011Cfu1gdJign9WUurGZoYHs"}
